Z||000000||Pheagey||11-02-2001||01:54 PM||||   Anyone know a good procedure for replacing the door bushings? (I have the book and have read it but...).<BR>   Also, are the E-Brake systems interchangable on all Fiero's?..<P>------------------<BR>"There is no replacement for displacement.Period"<BR>    -Mr.Frosty<P>'88 coupe, 5 speed<P>Http://www.LithiumEffects.com/car.html<P>Killed: '97 Civic LX Auto,<BR>Killed by: '93 Civic EX 5 speed,||||reg||5
Z||000001||Rodrv6||11-02-2001||04:10 PM||||Check the Ogre's Cave for door hinge info.  I think the E-brakes on the 84-87's are the same. I know the 88's are different.<P>------------------<BR>Rod Schneider, Woodstock, Ga.  <BR>White 88 GT :)||||reg||1
Z||000002||theogre||11-02-2001||07:51 PM||||84 to 87 essentially everything is interchangable. There are a few awkward bit but most is direct bolt in. In terms of brake all of it is the same.<P>In all honesty... if your cables are bad, buy new. Unless they are in very good shape, the odds are good you will damage used ones moving them. Check the ends of the cable jacket near the ends. The jacket is often broken there but you can't alwasy see it easily. I've got one like that now. You'd swear it was ok just looking at it.<P>The door pins are easy. Buy or borrow the tool listed in that cave article and they go very quickly. It's worth the $15 or so even if you only use it one time.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif">  <FONT COLOR="blue"><I><B>11-Sept-01, The day the world as we knew it ended.</B></I></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000003||Fierobruiser||11-03-2001||11:47 PM||||Try the hinge repair parts on this site or any other fasteners you might need for your Fiero.<P>------------------<BR>||||reg||1
